<section
	id="features"
	class="relative py-24 px-6 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] overflow-hidden"
>
	<div
		class="absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 -left-40 w-[500px] h-[500px] rounded-full blur-3xl opacity-20 pointer-events-none"
		style="background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--color-brand) 0%, transparent 60%);"
		aria-hidden="true"
	>
	</div>

	<div
		class="relative max-w-6xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-center"
	>
		<div>
			<span
				class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--color-brand)]"
				>El Ratio</span
			>
			<h2
				class="font-[var(--font-display)] mt-3 mb-4 text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight"
			>
				Lo que separa a
				<span
					class="bg-clip-text text-transparent"
					style="background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-brand), #c4a8ff);"
					>Completr</span
				>.
			</h2>
			<p
				class="m-0 text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-3"
			>
				El <strong class="text-[var(--color-fg)]">Ratio</strong> responde
				la pregunta que abre tu backlog cada noche: <em
					>¿qué juego ahora?</em
				>
				Combina la calificación de la comunidad con el tiempo promedio para
				terminarlo, en una sola métrica que premia los juegos que te dan más
				por cada hora que les inviertes.
			</p>
			<p class="m-0 text-[var(--color-fg-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
				Un 95 de 12 horas no pesa igual que un 95 de 80 horas. Uno cabe
				en una semana; el otro te pide medio mes. El Ratio te lo deja
				claro de un vistazo para que ordenes tu backlog según tu tiempo
				real, no según el hype.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="relative">
			<div
				class="relative max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-2xl p-6 border-2 border-[var(--color-brand)] overflow-hidden"
				style="background: linear-gradient(160deg, rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.18), transparent 60%), var(--color-surface);"
			>
				<div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
					<span
						class="flex items-center justify-center w-7 h-7 rounded-md font-display font-extrabold text-xs text-white"
						style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-brand), var(--color-brand-deep));"
						>C</span
					>
					<span
						class="text-[0.6875rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-brand)]"
						>Completr Score</span
					>
				</div>

				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 mb-1">
					<span
						class="text-6xl font-bold text-[var(--color-brand)] leading-none"
						>87.5</span
					>
					<span
						class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]"
						>Ratio</span
					>
				</div>
				<p
					class="m-0 mt-1 text-[0.6875rem] text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] leading-snug"
				>
					score relative to time invested by the community
				</p>

				<div
					class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-[var(--color-line)]/60 flex flex-col gap-2.5"
				>
					<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
						<span
							class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]"
							>Rating</span
						>
						<div class="flex items-center gap-1">
							<span class="text-[var(--color-brand)]">★★★★</span>
							<span class="text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">★</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
						<span
							class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]"
							>Duration</span
						>
						<span
							class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-fg)]"
							>18h <span
								class="text-[0.625rem] font-normal text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]"
								>avg</span
							></span
						>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
